      "decision": "KEEP",
      "actualVisualReason": "The current v4 scientist has no reversed notebook. Equal-volume tubes sit in three marked baths, with the same timing and control notes. Temperature labels and main controlled comparison are visible at 360; small auxiliary controls are legible at 680 but are not required reading for the independently supplied task. An ice motif is a cooling symbol rather than a numerical zero-degree assertion.",
      "positiveScienceReason": "Two cases require independent hypotheses and plans for temperature and pH, one changed factor, controlled enzyme/substrate/volume and timing, fresh independent repeats and initial-rate interpretation. Temperature means 2.0/6.0/0.4 ml over 40 s give 0.050/0.150/0.010 ml/s; repeated ranges 0.045-0.055, 0.145-0.155 and 0.0075-0.0125 are compatible with the tabulated data. The pH case means 1.3/3.1/1.9 ml over 30 s give 0.0433/0.1033/0.0633 ml/s. Color blanks, dilutions and return-to-temperature tests distinguish confounding, reversible temperature effects and damage; no universal enzyme optimum is claimed. Low peroxide, supervision and pressure release are specified.",
