      "positiveScienceReason": "Current fermentation-c1 defines 20 ml liquid, 0.2 g yeast and 2 percent m/V glucose (0.4 g available), temperature 30 degrees C, pressure 1 bar, dry corrected carbon-dioxide gas and 25.2 L/mol. Corrected 80 mmol/L ethanol times 0.020 L is 1.60 mmol; the 1:1 ethanol/carbon-dioxide reaction predicts 40.32 ml. Collected 38 ml is 94.246 percent and differs by 2.32 ml, within the explicit synthetic 90-100 percent collection interval. Triplicate ethanol 1.52/1.60/1.68 mmol predicts 38.304/40.32/42.336 ml versus collected 36/38/40 ml. Required glucose 0.8 mmol corresponds to about 0.144 g, below the available 0.4 g. Glycolysis net ATP is 4 minus 2 equals 2; fermentation regenerates NAD+ without additional ATP. The defined homofermentative lactate case has a 2:1 lactate/glucose ratio and no carbon dioxide; pH alone is not a lactate proof and heterogeneous fermentation can produce gas. Fresh aerated carbon dioxide without ethanol does not prove alcoholic fermentation. All data are declared synthetic; no actual culture or instrument recovery is certified.",
