      "actualVisualReason": "The illustration contrasts oxygen-dependent mitochondrial respiration and oxygen-free cytosolic lactate production. Stars are qualitative energy symbols, not numerical ATP counts; the native alternative text explicitly bounds them. Main pathways/products are recognizable at 360.",
      "positiveScienceReason": "Aerobic C6H12O6 plus 6 O2 to 6 CO2 plus 6 H2O conserves C6 H12 O18. Alcoholic 2 C2H6O plus 2 CO2 and homolactic 2 C3H6O3 each conserve the starting atoms; physiological lactate/proton notation is separately bounded. The supplied net 30 versus 2 ATP model requires 2 versus 30 glucose for 60 ATP, a 15-fold ratio; fresh 32 versus 2 requires 2 versus 32 for 64 ATP, ratio 16. Four respiration plus six lactate fermentations yield 132 ATP, 24 oxygen, 24 carbon dioxide and 12 lactate. Ten fermentations yield 20 ATP and 20 lactate, without oxygen use even if external oxygen is available when mitochondria are absent. Uncoupling invalidates the fixed aerobic ATP figure and does not automatically establish exclusive fermentation.",
