      "actualVisualReason": "Cooling, separation of raw chicken from ready food on distinct boards, and hand/surface cleaning are recognizable at 360; auxiliary longer captions require 680 for comfortable reading and are not compulsory task data. The magnified microbes are symbols, not a visible food-safety assay. Cooling caption explicitly rejects killing all microbes.",
      "positiveScienceReason": "Metabolism and multiplication are linked to food changes while transmission remains a distinct mechanism. Warm synthetic count 100 to 1600 is sixteen-fold; cold 100 to 120 is 1.2-fold and is not sterilization. Binary fission, budding, hyphal growth and spore spread are appropriately distinguished. A fluorescence model follows 100 to board 35 to ready-to-eat model 12, reduced to 1 by separate clean paths; the marker measures transport, not germ count, killing or infectious dose. A fresh hand route can bypass the board. Normal smell/appearance cannot certify safety, and spoilage organisms are not identical to pathogens. Unknown cultures and tasting are excluded; the candidate makes no real food-safety threshold or laboratory-trial claim.",
